Subject: [PATCH] mlx5e: probe 3-arg xsk_buff_get_metadata() and pass desc.options

Ubuntu linux-azure 6.8.0-1074.83 (LP: #2172890, Ubuntu 6.8.0-150.150)
backports upstream commit "xsk: honor XDP_TX_METADATA in zero-copy path"
(CVE-2026-90086), adding a third `u32 options` argument to
xsk_buff_get_metadata() in net/xdp_sock_drv.h.

MLNX OFED / DOCA's mlnx-ofed-kernel-dkms (3.2.3-3.5.0) still calls the
2-argument form in drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c,
failing DKMS builds with:
  error: too few arguments to function 'xsk_buff_get_metadata'

Add an MLNX_RDMA_TEST_CASE Autoconf probe in compat/config/rdma.m4
(HAVE_XSK_BUFF_GET_METADATA_3_PARAMS) and guard the 3-argument call in
tx.c on it so the patch works across both older kernels (including
6.8.0-1001..1073-azure, where XDP_TX_METADATA is already defined but
xsk_buff_get_metadata still takes 2 arguments) and newer kernels
(>= 6.8.0-1074-azure and 7.0+).

---
 compat/config/rdma.m4                               | 7 +++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compat/config/rdma.m4 b/compat/config/rdma.m4
--- a/compat/config/rdma.m4
+++ b/compat/config/rdma.m4
@@ -4015,6 +4015,13 @@
 		return 0;
 	])
 
+	MLNX_RDMA_TEST_CASE(HAVE_XSK_BUFF_GET_METADATA_3_PARAMS, [xsk_buff_get_metadata takes 3 parameters], [
+		#include <net/xdp_sock_drv.h>
+	],[
+		struct xsk_tx_metadata *meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(NULL, 0, 0);
+		return meta != NULL;
+	])
+
 	MLNX_RDMA_TEST_CASE(HAVE_XSK_TX_METADATA_OPS, [struct xsk_tx_metadata_ops is defined], [
 		#include <net/xdp_sock.h>
 	],[
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c
@@ -121,7 +121,11 @@
 #endif
 		xdptxd.len = desc.len;
 #ifdef HAVE_XSK_TX_METADATA_OPS
+#ifdef HAVE_XSK_BUFF_GET_METADATA_3_PARAMS
+		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, desc.addr, desc.options);
+#else
 		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, desc.addr);
+#endif
 #endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_XSK_BUFF_ALLOC
